xwikidoc.content:
{{include reference="ReleaseNotes.Code.Change.ChangeDisplayerVelocityMacros"/}}
{{velocity}} ## Inputs: ## - $changeItems ## - $displayEditLink #foreach ($item in $changeItems) #set ($changeDoc = $xwiki.getDocument($item)) #set ($changeObject = $changeDoc.getObject("ReleaseNotes.Code.Change.ChangeClass")) #generateDisplayEditLink($displayEditLink, $changeDoc) #set ($title = $services.rendering.escape("$!changeObject.getValue('title')", 'xwiki/2.1')) ## The title of a change is optional, so a change is only given a section of its own when it has one: a heading ## holding no text at all would leave an empty section in the release note, and an empty entry in the table of ## contents the release note template displays. The edit link then follows the summary, the only thing that ## displays such a change. #if ($title != '') === $title${displayEditLinkMarkup}=== #end ## Display the summary through the change document, so that its rich text is rendered in the context of that ## document rather than of this displayer, the way the change's own page renders it. ## The edit link of a change with no title reaches the summary line through a variable rather than through a ## directive closing that line: Velocity drops the newline ending a line that ends with a directive. The blank ## line that follows then closes the paragraph the summary is rendered in, which the screenshots below must not ## be part of: the gallery they are displayed in is a standalone macro and cannot be used inline. #set ($summaryEditLinkMarkup = '') #if ($title == '') #set ($summaryEditLinkMarkup = $displayEditLinkMarkup) #end $changeDoc.display('summary', 'view', $changeObject)$summaryEditLinkMarkup
#if ("$changeObject.getValue('screenshots')" != '') #displayScreenshots($changeObject, true, false)
#end #set ($description = $changeObject.getValue('description')) #if ("$!description" != '') [[${moreDetailsLabel}>>doc:$changeDoc.documentReference]] #end #end {{/velocity}}
